abstract: >-
  Code, data, figures, and checked manuscript sources for a passive
  pseudo-Hermitian driven Dirac impurity. Version 2.1 adds a causal full-k
  exceptional-point certificate for a stationary rotating drive, an SOC
  continuation family, and an exact zero-temperature finite-chain finite-U
  continuation with a common-contour N=10 to N=12 Rouche stability gate.
  These finite-chain results are not promoted to a continuum, thermodynamic,
  finite-temperature FDM-NRG, or strong-coupling Kondo theorem. The exact
  integrability claim remains restricted to the linearized equal-velocity
  scalar-hybridization submanifold.
keywords:
  - non-Hermitian physics
  - exceptional points
  - quantum impurity
  - Dirac bath
  - causal spectral density
  - Wigner-Smith delay
  - numerical renormalization group
  - block Wilson chain
  - Brouwer degree
  - Yang-Baxter equation
